59	// The ops `planSchedulerRun` emits, each a label-and-body mechanic the shell applies:
60	//   { kind: 'dedupe',  issue, reason }            close, task:obsolete
61	//   { kind: 'create',  pack, task, labels, body } a task's standing item
62	//   { kind: 'ready',   issue }                    task:blocked -> task:ready
63	//   { kind: 'reclaim', issue, reason }            task:executing -> task:ready
64	//   { kind: 'adopt',   request, title, body, … }  a marked issue becomes an item
65	//   { kind: 'supersede', issue, request, reason } a parked prior run of a re-ask
66	//   { kind: 'retire-orphan', issue, reason }      a standing item whose task is gone closes
67	//
68	// Beside the ops, `asked`: one `{ task, verdict, reason }` per task this run asked,
69	// `verdict` being `go`, `no` or `fail-open` — the run's log, and the whole record
70	// of a decline, since nothing durable is written for one.
71	//
72	// `items` is every `[claudinite-work]` issue the shell fetched (state=all back to
73	// the run-history horizon, open for the rest), each `{ number, title, body, state,
74	// labels, created_at, closed_at, updated_at }`. `stateOf(number)` answers the
75	// state of a `Blocked-by` target that may not be a work item at all; an unknown
76	// number is never treated as closed, so an unreadable blocker delays rather than
